@@section 1
@@title SQ-RDB Rustic Delight baked into its member, 2026-11-10 ([plan_rustic_fold_in.md](../plan_rustic_fold_in.md) 7, [rustic_delight.md](../rustic_delight.md) 5.14, TODO `creativedelight/members #55`)
@@date 2026-11-10
@@jars creativedelight
@@sources feature_writeup/plan_rustic_fold_in.md feature_writeup/rustic_delight.md
@@text
@@text Needs the 2026-11-10 Creative Delight jar (nests `backportedRustic-1.7.0-ce-19.2-02`) in `mods/`: full restart. Group A
@@text (superflat) unless noted. Baseline for -02: the pre-change dumps in `kubejs/exported/` (2026-11-09/10: 270 `rusticdelight`
@@text recipes in `recipes/all.csv`, items in `items_by_mod/rusticdelight.json`); copy them aside before the run's `/dumpall`.
@@text
@@text | ID | Group | Commands | Expected | If it fails |
@@text |---|---|---|---|---|
## SQ-RDB-01 | Rustic Delight with no rustic_upstream folder
@group A
@commands Boot with no `rustic_upstream/` folder (and no symlink) in the server dir; `grep -i "rustic\|Error occurred while handling event\|Couldn't parse\|Failed to load" logs/latest.log`
@pass `Done (`; no Rustic error or parse error for a `rusticdelight:` file; `/dumpall` items_by_mod/rusticdelight.json lists the same ids as the baseline (160 port ids plus blocks)
@fails A missing file: `bake_upstream.py --check`; a parse error: the bake rule for that folder
@from batches/r1111/a1.qb passed
bootexpect Done \(
shell ls -d rustic_upstream 2>&1; grep -iE "rustic" logs/latest.log | grep -iE "error|exception|couldn't parse|failed to load" | head -20; echo "rustic error lines: $(grep -iE 'rustic' logs/latest.log | grep -ciE "error|exception|couldn't parse|failed to load")" 
bootreject (?i)(Couldn't parse|Failed to load).*rusticdelight:

## SQ-RDB-02 | /dumpall: Rustic recipes, tags, loot and items equal the 11-10 baseline (kubejs/exported copied in by prep)
@group A
@commands `/dumpall`; compare `recipes/all.csv` rusticdelight rows, `tags/item_tags.json` and `tags/block_tags.json` rusticdelight entries, `loot_tables/` rusticdelight with the baseline
@pass Same recipe ids (270), same tag members, same loot tables
@fails Diff names the file; check its `bake_manifest.json` rules
@from batches/r1113/c4_a.qb
shell rm -rf rdb_base && cp -r kubejs/exported rdb_base && echo "baseline copied: $(grep -c '^rusticdelight:' rdb_base/recipes/all.csv) rusticdelight recipes"
> dumpall
waitlog \[dumpall\] (all \d+ dumps done|\d+/\d+ (dumps )?ok) 900
shell python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/rdb_compare.py rdb_base kubejs/exported rusticdelight
look every [rdb] line SAME (recipes 270); a DIFF names the entry: check its bake_manifest.json rule. items_by_mod on a dedicated server may lack client-only names (ids still compare)

