## SQ-RDB-05 | Rustic blocks from the 1.2.02 save keep their states
@group old world
@commands Save from the live pack with Rustic plates, crops, crates and potted wild coffee (as SQ-RD-03), opened on the -02 jar
@pass Every block keeps its state; no missing-registry warning for `rusticdelight:`
@fails Ids did not change, so a loss is a registry bug, not the bake
@from batches/r1115/p9_o2.qb passed
> zp9 bstate 200 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 202 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 204 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 206 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 208 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 210 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 212 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 214 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 216 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 218 -60 200
> zp9 bstate 220 -60 200
sleep 1
expect \[zp9\] bstate 200 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:pancakes\}\[facing=east,servings=4\]
expect \[zp9\] bstate 202 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:honey_pancakes\}\[facing=east,servings=7\]
expect \[zp9\] bstate 204 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:cotton\}\[age=3\]
expect \[zp9\] bstate 206 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:coffee\}\[age=4\]
expect \[zp9\] bstate 208 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:bell_peppers\}\[age=6\]
expect \[zp9\] bstate 210 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:bell_pepper_red_crate\}
expect \[zp9\] bstate 212 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:cotton_boll_crate\}
expect \[zp9\] bstate 214 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:potted_wild_coffee\}
expect \[zp9\] bstate 216 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:cherry_blossom_cheesecake\}\[bites=1,facing=north\]
expect \[zp9\] bstate 218 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:wild_coffee\}
expect \[zp9\] bstate 220 -60 200 Block\{rusticdelight:glowing_calamari_crate\}
shell echo "missing-registry lines naming rusticdelight: $(grep -ciE '(missing|unidentified|unknown).*rusticdelight' logs/latest.log)"; grep -iE "(missing|unidentified|unknown).*rusticdelight" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-240 | head -8

## SQ-RDB-06 | old rustic_upstream folder beside mods/ is ignored
@group A
@commands Boot again with an old `rustic_upstream/` folder (the 1.7.0 jar) left beside `mods/`
@pass Same as SQ-RDB-01: no duplicate pack, no error, folder ignored
@fails A pack named `rustic_upstream_assets` in the pack list: an old jar still nested
@from batches/r1111/a2.qb
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (?i)(Couldn't parse|Failed to load).*rusticdelight:
bootreject rustic_upstream_assets
shell ls -ld rustic_upstream; echo "rustic error lines: $(grep -iE 'rustic' logs/latest.log | grep -ciE "error|exception|couldn't parse|failed to load")"; grep -ciE 'rustic_upstream' logs/latest.log

